# Rules for the 100-continue response_line bypass test.
#
# 1201: the "final 200" rule on flow A (baseline). Fires normally.
# 1202: the "final 200" rule on flow B. Expected to fire once; on a
#       pre-fix build it does NOT fire (the bypass - the final
#       response's response line is never inspected).
# 1203: the "100 line" rule on flow B. Expected to fire once; on a
#       pre-fix build it double-alerts (HEADERS final run + LINE
#       non-terminal re-run after the rewind, against the stale
#       buffer).
alert tcp 10.0.0.2 any -> 10.0.0.1 10000 (msg:"100continue-response_line 200 response_line (baseline)"; sid:1201; rev:1; http.response_line; content:"200 OK";)
alert tcp 10.0.0.2 any -> 10.0.0.3 10001 (msg:"100continue-response_line 200 response_line"; sid:1202; rev:1; http.response_line; content:"200 OK";)
alert tcp 10.0.0.2 any -> 10.0.0.3 10001 (msg:"100continue-response_line 100 response_line"; sid:1203; rev:1; http.response_line; content:"100 Continue";)
